# Session-start git status

At the start of **every** conversation (before other work), run a full git
status check and use it to orient:

```bash
git status
git status -sb
git remote -v
git branch -vv
git log -5 --oneline
```

Note dirty files, branch vs `origin`, remotes, and recent commits before
planning or editing. Do not skip this because the task looks unrelated to git.
